{"type": "sena", "_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "The Shopping Spree", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Turn It Up!", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 8, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 7, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B1.3", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Identify and describe taste and style in music and fashion through a wider range of language in both work and social contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": " Writes well-organized texts or articles about explaining the rules and regulations in his/her industry using appropriate grammar, vocabulary, spelling coherence and cohesion, and different levels of formality. ", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": " Writes well-organized texts or articles about explaining the rules and regulations in his/her industry using appropriate grammar, vocabulary, spelling coherence and cohesion, and different levels of formality. ", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": " Writes well-organized texts or articles about explaining the rules and regulations in his/her industry using appropriate grammar, vocabulary, spelling coherence and cohesion, and different levels of formality. ", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": " Writes well-organized texts or articles about explaining the rules and regulations in his/her industry using appropriate grammar, vocabulary, spelling coherence and cohesion, and different levels of formality. ", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": " Writes well-organized texts or articles about explaining the rules and regulations in his/her industry using appropriate grammar, vocabulary, spelling coherence and cohesion, and different levels of formality. ", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": " Writes well-organized texts or articles about explaining the rules and regulations in his/her industry using appropriate grammar, vocabulary, spelling coherence and cohesion, and different levels of formality. ", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": " Writes well-organized texts or articles about explaining the rules and regulations in his/her industry using appropriate grammar, vocabulary, spelling coherence and cohesion, and different levels of formality. ", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": " Writes well-organized texts or articles about explaining the rules and regulations in his/her industry using appropriate grammar, vocabulary, spelling coherence and cohesion, and different levels of formality. ", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn8le07ob08re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Making Comparisons", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "We use <span class=\"italic\">as</span> + adjective/adverb +  <span class=\"italic\">as</span> to make comparisons when the things we are comparing are equal in some way.<br/> <br/>  We use  <span class=\"italic\">not as ... as</span> to make comparisons between things which aren't equal.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "These shoes are <span class=\"strong\">as ugly as</span> your old ones.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Her cat, Meenee, is <span class=\"strong\">not as friendly as</span> the one next door.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Her job does not pay <span class=\"strong\">as much as</span> his.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Superlatives ", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use the superlative to say what thing, person, or idea has the most of a particular quality within a group or of its kind.<br/><br/>Superlative adjectives normally come before any other adjectives.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":6,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Base Word\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Ending\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Example\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Words of one syllable ending in  <span class=\\\"italic\\\">e</span>.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Add <span class=\\\"italic\\\">-st</span> to the end of the word.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" <span class=\\\"italic\\\"> Whales are the  <span class=\\\"strong\\\">largest</span> animals on earth.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Words of one syllable, with one vowel and one consonant at the end. \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Double the consonant and add <span class=\\\"italic\\\">-est</span> to the end of the word.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> Who had the <span class=\\\"strong\\\">biggest</span> birthday party last year?</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Words of one syllable, with more than one vowel or more than one consonant at the end.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Add <span class=\\\"italic\\\">-est</span> to the end of the word.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" <span class=\\\"italic\\\"> That is the <span class=\\\"strong\\\">toughest</span> job in the company.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Words of two syllables, ending in <span class=\\\"italic\\\">y</span>.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Change <span class=\\\"italic\\\">y</span> to <span class=\\\"italic\\\">i</span>, and add <span class=\\\"italic\\\">-est</span> to the end of the word. \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> That is the <span class=\\\"strong\\\">silliest</span> thing I have ever done. </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Words of two syllables or more, not ending in <span class=\\\"italic\\\">y</span>.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Place <span class=\\\"italic\\\">\\\"the most\\\"</span> before the adjective.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> That is the <span class=\\\"strong\\\">most beautiful</span> dress in the store.</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "band", "type": "name"}, {"content": " a small group of musicians who play popular music together", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I can't wait to listen to the band tomorrow.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le07ob08aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": " These are words you hear in a conversation between friends.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "stage", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a raised platform where the performers stand", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: They might let us join them on stage.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le07ob08aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "crowd-surfing", "type": "name"}, {"content": " the process in which a person is passed overhead from person to person during a concert", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: There's even crowd-surfing.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le07ob08aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to plant", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to put or place yourself firmly or forcefully on a surface ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: My feet will be firmly planted on the ground.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le07ob08aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "Where on earth ... ? ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to ask exactly where", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Where on earth are you going to wear these?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le07ob08aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "replacement", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a thing that replaces something else", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: After I lost them on my trip, I've been looking for replacements.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le07ob08aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "diamante", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a sequin or rhinestone on a piece of clothing or accessory", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You bought pink stilettos with diamantes?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le07ob08aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "gate", "type": "name"}, {"content": " a place in a wall or a fence that has a movable part which can be opened or closed like a door", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: You can enter through gate 402, not 401 like the rest of us.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le07ob08aud08", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Write a 12-14-line dialogue about socializing and music.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Imagine you and a friend want to go to different music events on the weekend. You want to go to a rock concert. They want to attending a country music festival.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Describe where the events are, who is going and how you will get there.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Use comparatives and superlatives to support your argument. <span class=\"italic\">Examples: We should go to the rock concert in the city this weekend. The music is better and it is more popular than the country music festival. Country music festivals are not as exciting as rock concerts. I had the best time last year!</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Proofread your dialogue.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Read your dialogue aloud with a partner.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I write a dialogue about socializing and music.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I use comparatives and superlatives to support my viewpoint.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I read my dialogue about going to an event with a partner.", "type": "text"}]}], "labs": [{"id": 0, "_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"content": true, "type": "has_nav"}, {"content": true, "type": "has_exercise_controls"}]}], "type": "scholar", "exercises": [{"id": 0, "stimuli_ids": [0], "questions": [], "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": " I can write about socializing and music.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can make comparisons using <span class=\"italic\">as ... as</span> and <span class=\"italic\">not as</span>.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can compare two things or people and describe the quality of an object or a person. ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " What kind of music do you listen to?", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"content": " Have you ever been to a music festival or listened to a live band? When?", "type": "Free Header Item"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"content": "Welcome", "type": "group_name"}]}, {"content": {"correct_feedback": "Correct", "allowed_attempts": 2, "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "You have 2 tries", "type": "text"}, {"content": "you have 1 attempt left", "type": "text"}], "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "try again", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time", "type": "text"}]}, "type": "feedb